WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.427
This line creates out_host, a CPU array

00:00:03.427 --> 00:00:04.681
containing one zero.

00:00:09.181 --> 00:00:12.221
cuda.to_device copies the array into GPU

00:00:12.221 --> 00:00:15.768
memory. The original stays on the CPU.

00:00:20.268 --> 00:00:23.128
Numba compiles this Python kernel on the

00:00:23.128 --> 00:00:26.397
CPU. CUDA loads the compiled code onto the

00:00:26.397 --> 00:00:27.623
GPU when needed.

00:00:32.623 --> 00:00:35.369
One GPU thread runs the kernel. Its

00:00:35.369 --> 00:00:38.507
argument, out, is the array we just copied

00:00:38.507 --> 00:00:39.684
into GPU memory.

00:00:44.684 --> 00:00:47.369
Both arrays contain zero. Which array will

00:00:47.369 --> 00:00:49.287
change when this line runs?

00:00:57.787 --> 00:01:01.419
The GPU thread writes 42 to the GPU array.

00:01:01.419 --> 00:01:03.841
The CPU array still holds zero.

00:01:08.341 --> 00:01:10.944
Copy to host waits for the kernel to

00:01:10.944 --> 00:01:13.872
finish. It returns the value in a new CPU

00:01:13.872 --> 00:01:14.848
array called result.
